/* Verse Games: THE WHOLE COUNSEL · 2 Samuel chapters 1-5
   Verse text is filled/verified from the KJV by tools/fill-verses.js */
VG.registerBibleChapters("2samuel", [
{n:1, name:"David Mourns Saul", seal:{ref:"2 Samuel 1:27",verse:"How are the mighty fallen, and the weapons of war perished!"}, facts:["Did you know the young man who told David he had killed Saul expected a reward, but David had him executed for lifting his hand against the LORD's anointed (2 Samuel 1:14-16)?","Did you know David ordered his lament taught to the children of Judah as 'the use of the bow,' and it is preserved in the book of Jasher (2 Samuel 1:18)?","Did you know David's lament closes with the refrain 'How are the mighty fallen,' repeated at the opening, the middle, and the close of the song (2 Samuel 1:19, 1:25, 1:27)?"], questions:[
{q:"Where was David when the news of Saul's death reached him?", options:["Abiding in Ziklag, two days after the battle","Camping on Mount Gilboa","Hiding in the cave of Adullam","Dwelling in Hebron"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 1:1",verse:"Now it came to pass after the death of Saul, when David was returned from the slaughter of the Amalekites, and David had abode two days in Ziklag;", insight:"David was two days out of Ziklag when the news came; God often gives us a little distance before hard tidings."},
{q:"How did the messenger show he came with grievous news?", options:["His clothes rent, and earth upon his head","His sword broken and his shield dented","His horse lathered and his armor stripped","His face painted and his head uncovered"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 1:2",verse:"It came even to pass on the third day, that, behold, a man came out of the camp from Saul with his clothes rent, and earth upon his head: and so it was, when he came to David, that he fell to the earth, and did obeisance.", insight:"Rent clothes and dust on the head; grief had a language, and David read it at a glance."},
{q:"What tidings did the man bring from Israel?", options:["The people had fled, and Saul and Jonathan were dead","The Philistines had sued for peace","Saul had taken the throne again","Jonathan had fled to the Philistines"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 1:4",verse:"And David said unto him, How went the matter? I pray thee, tell me. And he answered, That the people are fled from the battle, and many of the people also are fallen and dead; and Saul and Jonathan his son are dead also.", insight:"The worst news came in a few plain words; honesty about loss is the first step toward mourning well."},
{q:"How did the young man say he found Saul on Mount Gilboa?", options:["Leaning upon his spear, with the chariots close upon him","Standing unhurt among his guard","Already dead among the slain","Fleeing toward the valley"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 1:6",verse:"And the young man that told him said, As I happened by chance upon mount Gilboa, behold, Saul leaned upon his spear; and, lo, the chariots and horsemen followed hard after him.", insight:"Saul leaned on the weapon that had served him for years; earthly strength makes a poor crutch at the end."},
{q:"What did Saul ask the young man to do?", options:["Stand upon him and slay him, for anguish was come upon him","Carry him down from the mountain","Bind up his wounds","Sound the retreat for his men"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 1:9",verse:"And he said unto me again, Stand, I pray thee, upon me, and slay me: for anguish is come upon me, because my life is yet whole in me.", insight:"'My life is yet whole in me,' Saul said, even while asking for death; despair speaks in contradictions."},
{q:"What did the young man take from Saul's body?", options:["The crown from his head and the bracelet from his arm","His sword and his shield","His royal robe and his signet","His bow and his quiver"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 1:10",verse:"So I stood upon him, and slew him, because I was sure that he could not live after that he was fallen: and I took the crown that was upon his head, and the bracelet that was on his arm, and have brought them hither unto my lord.", insight:"He gathered the tokens of a king to win favor; trophies taken from tragedy buy no one's blessing."},
{q:"What did David and his men do when they heard the news?", options:["Took hold of their clothes and rent them, and mourned and fasted","Armed themselves to avenge Saul","Sent for the elders to crown David","Fled deeper into the wilderness"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 1:11",verse:"Then David took hold on his clothes, and rent them; and likewise all the men that were with him:", insight:"They tore their clothes and wept for a king who had hunted David; grief can be generous even to an enemy."},
{q:"Until what time did they mourn, weep, and fast?", options:["Until even","Until midnight","For seven days","Until the new moon"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 1:12",verse:"And they mourned, and wept, and fasted until even, for Saul, and for Jonathan his son, and for the people of the LORD, and for the house of Israel; because they were fallen by the sword.", insight:"They mourned until evening; set grief its proper hours, and let the night bring rest."},
{q:"Who did the young man say he was?", options:["The son of a stranger, an Amalekite","A Benjamite of Saul's own tribe","A captain of Jonathan's guard","A Philistine deserter"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 1:13",verse:"And David said unto the young man that told him, Whence art thou? And he answered, I am the son of a stranger, an Amalekite.", insight:"A stranger from Amalek stood before David; the nations are always watching how God's people handle power."},
{q:"What searching question did David put to him?", options:["How wast thou not afraid to stretch forth thine hand to destroy the LORD's anointed?","Why didst thou not bring Saul alive?","Who sent thee to Ziklag with this tale?","Wherefore didst thou flee the battle?"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 1:14",verse:"And David said unto him, How wast thou not afraid to stretch forth thine hand to destroy the LORD’S anointed?", insight:"'The LORD's anointed'; David honored the office even when the man had failed, and would not excuse its violation."},
{q:"What sentence did David pronounce on the young man?", options:["Thy blood be upon thy head, and he was smitten and died","He was bound and sent to prison","He was fined and set free","He was made a captain in David's guard"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 1:16",verse:"And David said unto him, Thy blood be upon thy head; for thy mouth hath testified against thee, saying, I have slain the LORD’S anointed.", insight:"'Thy mouth hath testified against thee'; his own story condemned him, and David would not profit from the king's death."},
{q:"What did David compose over Saul and Jonathan?", options:["A lamentation","A victory song","A proverb for the elders","A prayer of thanksgiving"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 1:17",verse:"And David lamented with this lamentation over Saul and over Jonathan his son:", insight:"A lament, not a triumph song; David chose grief over gloating when his rival fell."},
{q:"What did David order to be taught to the children of Judah?", options:["The use of the bow","The songs of the temple","The laws of the kingdom","The names of the tribes"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 1:18",verse:"(Also he bade them teach the children of Judah the use of the bow: behold, it is written in the book of Jasher.)", insight:"He taught the next generation the weapon of the fallen; honor the fallen by learning what they knew."},
{q:"Where is David's lament said to be written?", options:["In the book of Jasher","In the chronicles of the kings","On the walls of Hebron","In the song of Moses"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 1:18",verse:"(Also he bade them teach the children of Judah the use of the bow: behold, it is written in the book of Jasher.)", insight:"Recorded in the book of Jasher; God keeps a book of remembrance for faithful grief."},
{q:"In which places did David forbid the news to be told?", options:["In Gath, and in the streets of Askelon","In Hebron and in Bethlehem","In Egypt and in Moab","In Dan and in Beersheba"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 1:20",verse:"Tell it not in Gath, publish it not in the streets of Askelon; lest the daughters of the Philistines rejoice, lest the daughters of the uncircumcised triumph.", insight:"Tell it not in Gath; David guarded God's honor among the nations even in his sorrow."},
{q:"What did David pronounce upon the mountains of Gilboa?", options:["Let there be no dew, neither let there be rain upon you","Let them be covered with forests","Let them be given to the Philistines","Let them be desolate forever"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 1:21",verse:"Ye mountains of Gilboa, let there be no dew, neither let there be rain, upon you, nor fields of offerings: for there the shield of the mighty is vilely cast away, the shield of Saul, as though he had not been anointed with oil.", insight:"No dew, no rain on Gilboa; the ground where the mighty fell bore the mark of David's grief."},
{q:"What did David say of Jonathan's bow and Saul's sword?", options:["The bow turned not back, and the sword returned not empty","They were broken in the battle","They were lost on the mountain","They were given to the Philistines"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 1:22",verse:"From the blood of the slain, from the fat of the mighty, the bow of Jonathan turned not back, and the sword of Saul returned not empty.", insight:"Their weapons never failed them; David praised their courage even as he mourned their end."},
{q:"How did David describe Saul and Jonathan in life?", options:["Lovely and pleasant, swifter than eagles, stronger than lions","Proud and cruel, feared by all Israel","Wise and gentle, loved by the poor","Rich and mighty, clothed in purple"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 1:23",verse:"Saul and Jonathan were lovely and pleasant in their lives, and in their death they were not divided: they were swifter than eagles, they were stronger than lions.", insight:"Lovely and pleasant in life, undivided in death; David remembered the best of them and let the rest go."},
{q:"With what had Saul clothed the daughters of Israel?", options:["Scarlet with other delights, and ornaments of gold","Sackcloth and ashes","White linen and silver","Armor and bronze"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 1:24",verse:"Ye daughters of Israel, weep over Saul, who clothed you in scarlet, with other delights, who put on ornaments of gold upon your apparel.", insight:"Scarlet and gold for the daughters of Israel; David called the nation to weep for the good the king had done."},
{q:"How did David describe Jonathan's love for him?", options:["Wonderful, passing the love of women","Steadfast as the mountains","Bright as the morning star","Deep as the sea"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 1:26",verse:"I am distressed for thee, my brother Jonathan: very pleasant hast thou been unto me: thy love to me was wonderful, passing the love of women.", insight:"A love passing the love of women; true friendship is one of God's richest gifts, and David named it plainly."}
]},
{n:2, name:"David Anointed in Hebron", seal:{ref:"2 Samuel 2:4",verse:"And the men of Judah came, and there they anointed David king over the house of Judah. And they told David, saying, That the men of Jabesh-gilead were they that buried Saul."}, facts:["Did you know David would not move to Judah until he had asked the LORD, and the answer was one word: Hebron (2 Samuel 2:1)?","Did you know the battle at Gibeon began as a contest, with twelve young men on each side arising to 'play' before the armies, and each pair fell together by the sword (2 Samuel 2:14-16)?","Did you know the field where they died was named Helkathhazzurim, the field of swords (2 Samuel 2:16)?"], questions:[
{q:"What did David do before going up into the cities of Judah?", options:["Enquired of the LORD","Sent spies to Hebron","Gathered his captains","Offered a sacrifice at Ziklag"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 2:1",verse:"And it came to pass after this, that David enquired of the LORD, saying, Shall I go up into any of the cities of Judah? And the LORD said unto him, Go up. And David said, Whither shall I go up? And he said, Unto Hebron.", insight:"He enquired of the LORD first; the throne came to the man who would not move without God."},
{q:"Where did the LORD tell David to go?", options:["Unto Hebron","Unto Jerusalem","Unto Bethlehem","Unto Gibeon"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 2:1",verse:"And it came to pass after this, that David enquired of the LORD, saying, Shall I go up into any of the cities of Judah? And the LORD said unto him, Go up. And David said, Whither shall I go up? And he said, Unto Hebron.", insight:"One word, Hebron; God's guidance is often simpler than our questions."},
{q:"Which two wives went up with David to Hebron?", options:["Ahinoam the Jezreelitess, and Abigail the wife of Nabal the Carmelite","Michal and Maacah","Haggith and Abital","Eglah and Rizpah"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 2:2",verse:"So David went up thither, and his two wives also, Ahinoam the Jezreelitess, and Abigail Nabal’s wife the Carmelite.", insight:"Both wives went with him; the household shares the journey when God moves a man."},
{q:"Where did David's men settle with their households?", options:["In the cities of Hebron","In the wilderness of Ziph","In the towns of Gilead","In the villages of Bethlehem"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 2:3",verse:"And his men that were with him did David bring up, every man with his household: and they dwelt in the cities of Hebron.", insight:"Every man with his household; God provides room for the families of those who follow Him."},
{q:"Who anointed David king over the house of Judah?", options:["The men of Judah","The elders of Israel","The priests of the LORD","The captains of his army"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 2:4",verse:"And the men of Judah came, and there they anointed David king over the house of Judah. And they told David, saying, That the men of Jabesh-gilead were they that buried Saul.", insight:"The men of Judah anointed him; God's promise came through the hands of His people."},
{q:"For what kindness did David bless the men of Jabeshgilead?", options:["They had buried Saul","They had hidden David's spies","They had fed his army","They had warned him of Abner"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 2:5",verse:"And David sent messengers unto the men of Jabesh-gilead, and said unto them, Blessed be ye of the LORD, that ye have shewed this kindness unto your lord, even unto Saul, and have buried him.", insight:"They buried Saul; David blessed the men who honored his enemy, for kindness is never wasted."},
{q:"Who made Ishbosheth king over Israel?", options:["Abner the son of Ner, the captain of Saul's host","Joab the son of Zeruiah","The elders of Benjamin","The Philistine lords"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 2:8",verse:"But Abner the son of Ner, captain of Saul’s host, took Ish-bosheth the son of Saul, and brought him over to Mahanaim;", insight:"Abner set up Saul's son; human schemes can crown a king but cannot give him God's blessing."},
{q:"Where did Abner set up Ishbosheth's throne?", options:["At Mahanaim","At Gibeon","At Jerusalem","At Shechem"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 2:8",verse:"But Abner the son of Ner, captain of Saul’s host, took Ish-bosheth the son of Saul, and brought him over to Mahanaim;", insight:"Mahanaim, beyond the Jordan; the rival throne began in exile from God's chosen city."},
{q:"Which house followed David?", options:["The house of Judah","The house of Benjamin","The house of Ephraim","The house of Joseph"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 2:10",verse:"Ish-bosheth Saul’s son was forty years old when he began to reign over Israel, and reigned two years. But the house of Judah followed David.", insight:"The house of Judah followed David; God's anointed always finds those who recognize God's hand."},
{q:"How long did Ishbosheth reign?", options:["Two years","Seven years","Forty years","Six months"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 2:10",verse:"Ish-bosheth Saul’s son was forty years old when he began to reign over Israel, and reigned two years. But the house of Judah followed David.", insight:"Two years against David's growing strength; what God has not planted withers quickly."},
{q:"Where did the forces of Abner and Joab meet?", options:["By the pool of Gibeon","At the ford of Jordan","In the valley of Rephaim","On the hill of Ammah"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 2:13",verse:"And Joab the son of Zeruiah, and the servants of David, went out, and met together by the pool of Gibeon: and they sat down, the one on the one side of the pool, and the other on the other side of the pool.", insight:"They sat on either side of the pool; sometimes enemies face each other across still water before the storm."},
{q:"How many young men arose to play before the armies?", options:["Twelve of Benjamin and twelve of David's servants","Ten and ten","Thirty and thirty","Seven and seven"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 2:15",verse:"Then there arose and went over by number twelve of Benjamin, which pertained to Ish-bosheth the son of Saul, and twelve of the servants of David.", insight:"Twelve against twelve; the 'play' turned deadly, and games with death are never games."},
{q:"What was the place of that slaughter called?", options:["Helkathhazzurim","Baalperazim","The valley of Rephaim","The hill of Ammah"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 2:16",verse:"And they caught every one his fellow by the head, and thrust his sword in his fellow’s side; so they fell down together: wherefore that place was called Helkath-hazzurim, which is in Gibeon.", insight:"Helkathhazzurim, the field of swords; every pair fell together, and the ground kept the name."},
{q:"How is Asahel's swiftness described?", options:["Light of foot as a wild roe","Swift as an eagle","Fleet as the wind","Fast as a chariot horse"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 2:18",verse:"And there were three sons of Zeruiah there, Joab, and Abishai, and Asahel: and Asahel was as light of foot as a wild roe.", insight:"Light of foot as a wild roe; speed is a gift, but Asahel's speed outran his wisdom."},
{q:"How did Abner kill Asahel?", options:["With the hinder end of his spear, under the fifth rib","With a sword through his helmet","With an arrow from afar","With a stone from his sling"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 2:23",verse:"Howbeit he refused to turn aside: wherefore Abner with the hinder end of the spear smote him under the fifth rib, that the spear came out behind him; and he fell down there, and died in the same place: and it came to pass, that as many as came to the place where Asahel fell down and died stood still.", insight:"He warned him twice before he struck; even in battle, Abner gave the young man a chance to turn."},
{q:"What did Abner cry out to Joab at sunset?", options:["Shall the sword devour for ever?","Surrender thy men to me","Flee before the Benjamites","Spare my life, I pray thee"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 2:26",verse:"Then Abner called to Joab, and said, Shall the sword devour for ever? knowest thou not that it will be bitterness in the latter end? how long shall it be then, ere thou bid the people return from following their brethren?", insight:"'Shall the sword devour for ever?' The man who started the contest was the first to plead for it to end."},
{q:"How did Joab stop the pursuit?", options:["He blew a trumpet, and the people stood still","He called a council of war","He sent a messenger to David","He lit a signal fire"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 2:28",verse:"So Joab blew a trumpet, and all the people stood still, and pursued after Israel no more, neither fought they any more.", insight:"One trumpet blast stopped the slaughter; a leader knows when to call his people back."},
{q:"How many of David's servants were missing after the battle?", options:["Nineteen men and Asahel","Three hundred and threescore","Forty and two","Twelve young men"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 2:30",verse:"And Joab returned from following Abner: and when he had gathered all the people together, there lacked of David’s servants nineteen men and Asahel.", insight:"Nineteen men and Asahel; David's side counted its dead by name, not by number."},
{q:"How many of Benjamin and Abner's men fell?", options:["Three hundred and threescore men","Nineteen men","Twelve young men","Forty and two"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 2:31",verse:"But the servants of David had smitten of Benjamin, and of Abner’s men, so that three hundred and threescore men died.", insight:"Three hundred and sixty fell; the contest Abner proposed cost his side dearly."},
{q:"Where was Asahel buried?", options:["In his father's sepulchre in Bethlehem","In the field of Gibeon","At Mahanaim","In Hebron"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 2:32",verse:"And they took up Asahel, and buried him in the sepulchre of his father, which was in Bethlehem. And Joab and his men went all night, and they came to Hebron at break of day.", insight:"Buried in his father's tomb at Bethlehem; Joab marched all night to lay his brother to rest at home."}
]},
{n:3, name:"Abner Turns to David", seal:{ref:"2 Samuel 3:38",verse:"And the king said unto his servants, Know ye not that there is a prince and a great man fallen this day in Israel?"}, facts:["Did you know Abner turned to David after Ishbosheth accused him over Saul's concubine Rizpah, and the frightened king could not answer him a word (2 Samuel 3:7-11)?","Did you know David demanded Michal as the price of peace with Abner, and her husband Phaltiel walked weeping behind her all the way to Bahurim (2 Samuel 3:13-16)?","Did you know David honored the murdered Abner with a lament and a fast till sunset, calling him a prince and a great man fallen in Israel (2 Samuel 3:33-38)?"], questions:[
{q:"How did the long war between the houses of Saul and David go?", options:["David waxed stronger and stronger, and the house of Saul waxed weaker and weaker","Both houses grew equally strong","The house of Saul prevailed at first","David's house nearly perished"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 3:1",verse:"Now there was long war between the house of Saul and the house of David: but David waxed stronger and stronger, and the house of Saul waxed weaker and weaker.", insight:"God's anointed grew stronger while the rival house faded; time is on the side of God's purposes."},
{q:"Who was David's firstborn son in Hebron?", options:["Amnon, of Ahinoam the Jezreelitess","Absalom, of Maacah","Adonijah, of Haggith","Chileab, of Abigail"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 3:2",verse:"And unto David were sons born in Hebron: and his firstborn was Amnon, of Ahinoam the Jezreelitess;", insight:"Amnon the firstborn; the list of sons begins with promise, though not all promises end well."},
{q:"How many sons were born to David in Hebron?", options:["Six","Three","Twelve","Eleven"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 3:5",verse:"And the sixth, Ithream, by Eglah David’s wife. These were born to David in Hebron.", insight:"Six sons in Hebron; the growing household mirrored the growing kingdom."},
{q:"Who was Absalom's mother?", options:["Maacah, the daughter of Talmai king of Geshur","Abigail the Carmelitess","Haggith","Eglah"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 3:3",verse:"And his second, Chileab, of Abigail the wife of Nabal the Carmelite; and the third, Absalom the son of Maacah the daughter of Talmai king of Geshur;", insight:"Maacah, a king's daughter from Geshur; royal marriages wove foreign threads into David's house."},
{q:"What charge did Ishbosheth bring against Abner?", options:["That he had gone in unto his father's concubine","That he had stolen from the treasury","That he had conspired with David","That he had fled from battle"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 3:7",verse:"And Saul had a concubine, whose name was Rizpah, the daughter of Aiah: and Ish-bosheth said to Abner, Wherefore hast thou gone in unto my father’s concubine?", insight:"A charge over Saul's concubine Rizpah; accusing the strong man proved the weak king's undoing."},
{q:"What did the angry Abner swear the LORD would do?", options:["Translate the kingdom from the house of Saul, and set up the throne of David","Destroy Ishbosheth utterly","Give him the kingdom himself","Make peace between the houses"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 3:9",verse:"So do God to Abner, and more also, except, as the LORD hath sworn to David, even so I do to him;", insight:"Abner swore to transfer the kingdom; even his anger served God's settled purpose for David."},
{q:"From where to where would David's throne be established?", options:["From Dan even to Beersheba","From Egypt to the Euphrates","From Gilead to the sea","From Hebron to Jerusalem"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 3:10",verse:"To translate the kingdom from the house of Saul, and to set up the throne of David over Israel and over Judah, from Dan even to Beer-sheba.", insight:"From Dan to Beersheba; the whole land, north to south, was promised to David's throne."},
{q:"Why could Ishbosheth not answer Abner a word?", options:["Because he feared him","Because he was guilty","Because his counselors stopped him","Because he had fled"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 3:11",verse:"And he could not answer Abner a word again, because he feared him.", insight:"Fear silenced the king; a throne held by another man's strength is no throne at all."},
{q:"What condition did David set for a league with Abner?", options:["Bring Michal Saul's daughter before seeing his face","Pay a tribute of silver","Disband his army first","Swear by the LORD"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 3:13",verse:"And he said, Well; I will make a league with thee: but one thing I require of thee, that is, Thou shalt not see my face, except thou first bring Michal Saul’s daughter, when thou comest to see my face.", insight:"Bring Michal first; David would take back what was his before he trusted Abner's offer."},
{q:"From whom was Michal taken and sent to David?", options:["Phaltiel the son of Laish","Ishbosheth the son of Saul","Abner the son of Ner","A captain of Benjamin"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 3:15",verse:"And Ish-bosheth sent, and took her from her husband, even from Phaltiel the son of Laish.", insight:"Taken from Phaltiel; restoring David's wife cost another man his tears."},
{q:"How did Michal's husband react as she was taken?", options:["He went along weeping behind her to Bahurim","He fought Abner's men","He fled to the Philistines","He blessed her and returned"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 3:16",verse:"And her husband went with her along weeping behind her to Bahurim. Then said Abner unto him, Go, return. And he returned.", insight:"He wept all the way to Bahurim; the politics of kings are paid for in private grief."},
{q:"What did Abner say to the weeping husband?", options:["Go, return","Take up thy sword","Follow her to Hebron","Weep not, she is safe"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 3:16",verse:"And her husband went with her along weeping behind her to Bahurim. Then said Abner unto him, Go, return. And he returned.", insight:"'Go, return'; two cold words ended years of marriage, and the man obeyed."},
{q:"What did Abner urge the elders of Israel to do?", options:["Make David king now, for the LORD had spoken of him","Wait until Ishbosheth died","Crown Abner instead","Make peace with the Philistines"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 3:18",verse:"Now then do it: for the LORD hath spoken of David, saying, By the hand of my servant David I will save my people Israel out of the hand of the Philistines, and out of the hand of all their enemies.", insight:"'The LORD hath spoken of David'; even Abner confessed what Israel had long known."},
{q:"How many men came with Abner to David in Hebron?", options:["Twenty men","Twelve captains","Three hundred men","Seven elders"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 3:20",verse:"So Abner came to David to Hebron, and twenty men with him. And David made Abner and the men that were with him a feast.", insight:"Twenty men came in peace; reconciliation walks in quietly, not with an army."},
{q:"What did David do for Abner and his men?", options:["Made them a feast","Gave them gifts of gold","Anointed them as captains","Sent them to the battle"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 3:20",verse:"So Abner came to David to Hebron, and twenty men with him. And David made Abner and the men that were with him a feast.", insight:"David made them a feast; he welcomed the defector with a table, not a tribunal."},
{q:"What did Abner promise as David sent him away in peace?", options:["To gather all Israel unto his lord the king","To slay Ishbosheth himself","To bring the ark to Hebron","To serve as David's captain"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 3:21",verse:"And Abner said unto David, I will arise and go, and will gather all Israel unto my lord the king, that they may make a league with thee, and that thou mayest reign over all that thine heart desireth. And David sent Abner away; and he went in peace.", insight:"He went in peace to gather all Israel; the kingdom was nearly whole when murder broke it."},
{q:"What did Joab accuse Abner of when he heard of the visit?", options:["Coming to deceive David and spy out his goings","Plotting to kill David","Stealing the spoil of the troops","Bribing David's servants"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 3:25",verse:"Thou knowest Abner the son of Ner, that he came to deceive thee, and to know thy going out and thy coming in, and to know all that thou doest.", insight:"Joab called him a spy; suspicion can murder peace faster than any sword."},
{q:"From where did Joab's messengers bring Abner back?", options:["From the well of Sirah","From the pool of Gibeon","From Mahanaim","From Bahurim"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 3:26",verse:"And when Joab was come out from David, he sent messengers after Abner, which brought him again from the well of Sirah: but David knew it not.", insight:"Brought back from the well of Sirah without David's knowledge; secret errands often serve secret revenge."},
{q:"How did Joab kill Abner?", options:["He smote him under the fifth rib in the gate","He slew him with a sword in battle","He had him stoned by the people","He poisoned his cup at the feast"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 3:27",verse:"And when Abner was returned to Hebron, Joab took him aside in the gate to speak with him quietly, and smote him there under the fifth rib, that he died, for the blood of Asahel his brother.", insight:"Under the fifth rib, as Abner had slain Asahel; revenge dressed itself as justice."},
{q:"What did David say of Abner that day?", options:["A prince and a great man is fallen this day in Israel","A traitor has received his reward","The LORD has judged the wicked","My enemy is cut off"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 3:38",verse:"And the king said unto his servants, Know ye not that there is a prince and a great man fallen this day in Israel?", insight:"A prince and a great man fallen; David honored the dead even when his own house had killed him."}
]},
{n:4, name:"The Murder of Ishbosheth", seal:{ref:"2 Samuel 4:11",verse:"How much more, when wicked men have slain a righteous person in his own house upon his bed? shall I not therefore now require his blood of your hand, and take you away from the earth?"}, facts:["Did you know Mephibosheth, Jonathan's son, was crippled at five years old when his nurse fell while fleeing at the news of Saul and Jonathan's death (2 Samuel 4:4)?","Did you know Ishbosheth's assassins entered his house pretending to fetch wheat and struck him under the fifth rib as he lay on his bed at noon (2 Samuel 4:5-7)?","Did you know David called Ishbosheth 'a righteous person' and had the murderers' hands and feet cut off and their bodies hanged over the pool in Hebron (2 Samuel 4:11-12)?"], questions:[
{q:"How did Ishbosheth receive the news of Abner's death?", options:["His hands were feeble, and all the Israelites were troubled","He rejoiced and made a feast","He fled to the Philistines","He crowned himself at once"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 4:1",verse:"And when Saul’s son heard that Abner was dead in Hebron, his hands were feeble, and all the Israelites were troubled.", insight:"His hands were feeble; when the strong man falls, the weak king's courage falls with him."},
{q:"Who were the two captains of Ishbosheth's bands?", options:["Baanah and Rechab, the sons of Rimmon","Joab and Abishai","Abner and Asahel","Hushai and Zadok"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 4:2",verse:"And Saul’s son had two men that were captains of bands: the name of the one was Baanah, and the name of the other Rechab, the sons of Rimmon a Beerothite, of the children of Benjamin: (for Beeroth also was reckoned to Benjamin:", insight:"Baanah and Rechab, captains of bands; the men closest to the throne became its betrayers."},
{q:"Of which tribe were Baanah and Rechab?", options:["Benjamin","Judah","Ephraim","Levi"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 4:2",verse:"And Saul’s son had two men that were captains of bands: the name of the one was Baanah, and the name of the other Rechab, the sons of Rimmon a Beerothite, of the children of Benjamin: (for Beeroth also was reckoned to Benjamin:", insight:"Of Benjamin, Saul's own tribe; treachery cut closest to home."},
{q:"At what time of day did they come to Ishbosheth's house?", options:["About the heat of the day","At midnight","At the break of day","In the evening"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 4:5",verse:"And the sons of Rimmon the Beerothite, Rechab and Baanah, went, and came about the heat of the day to the house of Ish-bosheth, who lay on a bed at noon.", insight:"About the heat of the day; murder came at noon, when guards grow drowsy."},
{q:"What was Ishbosheth doing when they came?", options:["Lying on a bed at noon","Eating with his captains","Praying in his chamber","Reviewing his troops"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 4:5",verse:"And the sons of Rimmon the Beerothite, Rechab and Baanah, went, and came about the heat of the day to the house of Ish-bosheth, who lay on a bed at noon.", insight:"Lying on his bed at noon; the king at rest was the king unguarded."},
{q:"Who was Mephibosheth?", options:["Jonathan's son, lame on both his feet","Saul's youngest son","Abner's nephew","A captain of Benjamin"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 4:4",verse:"And Jonathan, Saul’s son, had a son that was lame of his feet. He was five years old when the tidings came of Saul and Jonathan out of Jezreel, and his nurse took him up, and fled: and it came to pass, as she made haste to flee, that he fell, and became lame. And his name was Mephibosheth.", insight:"Jonathan's lame son; the house of Saul was reduced to a crippled child in hiding."},
{q:"How old was Mephibosheth when he became lame?", options:["Five years old","Twelve years old","Three years old","Seven years old"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 4:4",verse:"And Jonathan, Saul’s son, had a son that was lame of his feet. He was five years old when the tidings came of Saul and Jonathan out of Jezreel, and his nurse took him up, and fled: and it came to pass, as she made haste to flee, that he fell, and became lame. And his name was Mephibosheth.", insight:"Five years old when the tidings came; a child's life was broken by news he did not cause."},
{q:"How did the murderers get into the house?", options:["As though they would fetch wheat","Disguised as beggars","Through a window at night","Bribing the doorkeeper"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 4:6",verse:"And they came thither into the midst of the house, as though they would have fetched wheat; and they smote him under the fifth rib: and Rechab and Baanah his brother escaped.", insight:"Pretending to fetch wheat; treason often wears the clothes of ordinary business."},
{q:"Where did they smite Ishbosheth?", options:["Under the fifth rib","In the neck","Through the heart","In the side with a sword"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 4:6",verse:"And they came thither into the midst of the house, as though they would have fetched wheat; and they smote him under the fifth rib: and Rechab and Baanah his brother escaped.", insight:"Under the fifth rib; the same deadly spot where Abner fell, and where Asahel fell before him."},
{q:"What did they carry away from the house?", options:["His head","His crown","His signet ring","His royal robe"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 4:7",verse:"For when they came into the house, he lay on his bed in his bedchamber, and they smote him, and slew him, and beheaded him, and took his head, and gat them away through the plain all night.", insight:"They took his head through the plain all night; murder travels far to buy favor."},
{q:"How far did they journey with the head?", options:["Through the plain all night","To the land of Egypt","Across the Jordan at dawn","Three days into the wilderness"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 4:7",verse:"For when they came into the house, he lay on his bed in his bedchamber, and they smote him, and slew him, and beheaded him, and took his head, and gat them away through the plain all night.", insight:"All night through the plain; evil is tireless when it expects a reward."},
{q:"What did they claim David would see in the deed?", options:["That the LORD had avenged his lord the king of Saul and his seed","That the people loved David","That Abner's death was justified","That Ishbosheth had been a tyrant"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 4:8",verse:"And they brought the head of Ish-bosheth unto David to Hebron, and said to the king, Behold the head of Ish-bosheth the son of Saul thine enemy, which sought thy life; and the LORD hath avenged my lord the king this day of Saul, and of his seed.", insight:"They called it the LORD's vengeance; men baptize their crimes with holy names."},
{q:"What did they say Ishbosheth had done to David?", options:["Sought thy life","Stolen thy wives","Burned thy cities","Cursed thy name"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 4:8",verse:"And they brought the head of Ish-bosheth unto David to Hebron, and said to the king, Behold the head of Ish-bosheth the son of Saul thine enemy, which sought thy life; and the LORD hath avenged my lord the king this day of Saul, and of his seed.", insight:"'Which sought thy life'; they dressed their treason as loyalty to David."},
{q:"By what did David swear when he answered them?", options:["As the LORD liveth, who hath redeemed my soul out of all adversity","By the throne of his father","By the ark of God","By his own right hand"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 4:9",verse:"And David answered Rechab and Baanah his brother, the sons of Rimmon the Beerothite, and said unto them, As the LORD liveth, who hath redeemed my soul out of all adversity,", insight:"The LORD who redeemed his soul; David's answer came from what God had done, not what men had offered."},
{q:"What earlier deed did David remind them of?", options:["The Amalekite at Ziklag who claimed to have slain Saul","The slaying of Goliath","The sparing of Saul in the cave","The death of Abner"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 4:10",verse:"When one told me, saying, Behold, Saul is dead, thinking to have brought good tidings, I took hold of him, and slew him in Ziklag, who thought that I would have given him a reward for his tidings:", insight:"He reminded them of Ziklag; David's justice did not change with his fortunes."},
{q:"What did David call Ishbosheth?", options:["A righteous person","A foolish king","A son of Belial","A man of blood"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 4:11",verse:"How much more, when wicked men have slain a righteous person in his own house upon his bed? shall I not therefore now require his blood of your hand, and take you away from the earth?", insight:"'A righteous person'; David would not let murderers rewrite the dead man's name."},
{q:"What did David say he would require of the murderers?", options:["His blood of their hand","A ransom of silver","Their service forever","Exile from the land"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 4:11",verse:"How much more, when wicked men have slain a righteous person in his own house upon his bed? shall I not therefore now require his blood of your hand, and take you away from the earth?", insight:"'Require his blood of your hand'; God keeps accounts that men cannot settle with excuses."},
{q:"What did David command his young men to do?", options:["Slay them","Bind them in prison","Whip them publicly","Send them to the mines"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 4:12",verse:"And David commanded his young men, and they slew them, and cut off their hands and their feet, and hanged them up over the pool in Hebron. But they took the head of Ish-bosheth, and buried it in the sepulchre of Abner in Hebron.", insight:"Justice was swift; David would not build his throne on the blood of the innocent."},
{q:"What was done with the bodies of the murderers?", options:["Their hands and feet were cut off, and they were hanged over the pool in Hebron","They were buried with honors","They were cast into the wilderness","They were burned with fire"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 4:12",verse:"And David commanded his young men, and they slew them, and cut off their hands and their feet, and hanged them up over the pool in Hebron. But they took the head of Ish-bosheth, and buried it in the sepulchre of Abner in Hebron.", insight:"Hanged over the pool in Hebron; the whole city saw what David thought of treachery."},
{q:"Where did the Beerothites flee?", options:["To Gittaim","To Egypt","To the Philistines","To Moab"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 4:3",verse:"And the Beerothites fled to Gittaim, and were sojourners there until this day.)", insight:"They fled to Gittaim and sojourned there; even the murderers' hometown scattered before the storm."}
]},
{n:5, name:"David King of All Israel", seal:{ref:"2 Samuel 5:10",verse:"And David went on, and grew great, and the LORD God of hosts was with him."}, facts:["Did you know David was thirty when he became king and reigned forty years: seven and a half in Hebron over Judah, and thirty-three in Jerusalem over all Israel (2 Samuel 5:4-5)?","Did you know Hiram king of Tyre sent cedar trees, carpenters, and masons to build David a house, a foreign king honoring the new king of Israel (2 Samuel 5:11)?","Did you know David named the battlefield Baalperazim, the master of breaches, because the LORD broke through his enemies like bursting waters (2 Samuel 5:20)?"], questions:[
{q:"Who came to David at Hebron?", options:["All the tribes of Israel","Only the men of Judah","The elders of Benjamin","The priests and Levites"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 5:1",verse:"Then came all the tribes of Israel to David unto Hebron, and spake, saying, Behold, we are thy bone and thy flesh.", insight:"All the tribes came; the divided kingdom began to heal around God's anointed."},
{q:"What did the tribes say of themselves to David?", options:["Behold, we are thy bone and thy flesh","We are thy servants forever","We bring thee tribute","We seek thy protection"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 5:1",verse:"Then came all the tribes of Israel to David unto Hebron, and spake, saying, Behold, we are thy bone and thy flesh.", insight:"'Thy bone and thy flesh'; they claimed kinship with the king they had once rejected."},
{q:"What did they remind David he had done under Saul?", options:["Led out and brought in Israel","Slain Goliath alone","Played the harp for Saul","Hidden in the wilderness"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 5:2",verse:"Also in time past, when Saul was king over us, thou wast he that leddest out and broughtest in Israel: and the LORD said to thee, Thou shalt feed my people Israel, and thou shalt be a captain over Israel.", insight:"He had led them out and in while Saul reigned; faithful service in obscurity prepares a man for the throne."},
{q:"What had the LORD said of David?", options:["Thou shalt feed my people Israel, and thou shalt be a captain over Israel","Thou shalt build me an house","Thou shalt number the people","Thou shalt judge the nations"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 5:2",verse:"Also in time past, when Saul was king over us, thou wast he that leddest out and broughtest in Israel: and the LORD said to thee, Thou shalt feed my people Israel, and thou shalt be a captain over Israel.", insight:"Feed my people and be their captain; kingship in God's eyes is shepherding, not ruling."},
{q:"What did the elders of Israel do at Hebron?", options:["Made a league with David and anointed him king over Israel","Crowned him with Saul's crown","Gave him the ark of God","Built him a palace"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 5:3",verse:"So all the elders of Israel came to the king to Hebron; and king David made a league with them in Hebron before the LORD: and they anointed David king over Israel.", insight:"A league and an anointing; covenant bound the king and the people together before God."},
{q:"How old was David when he began to reign?", options:["Thirty years old","Twenty-five years old","Forty years old","Twenty years old"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 5:4",verse:"David was thirty years old when he began to reign, and he reigned forty years.", insight:"Thirty years old; the shepherd boy waited long, and God was never late."},
{q:"How long did David reign in all?", options:["Forty years","Thirty-three years","Seven years","Fifty years"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 5:4",verse:"David was thirty years old when he began to reign, and he reigned forty years.", insight:"Forty years; a full generation under one king, the measure of God's patience with His people."},
{q:"How long did David reign in Hebron over Judah?", options:["Seven years and six months","Two years","Twelve years","Forty years"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 5:5",verse:"In Hebron he reigned over Judah seven years and six months: and in Jerusalem he reigned thirty and three years over all Israel and Judah.", insight:"Seven years and six months in Hebron; the partial kingdom prepared him for the whole."},
{q:"How long did he reign in Jerusalem over all Israel and Judah?", options:["Thirty and three years","Seven years","Twenty years","Forty years"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 5:5",verse:"In Hebron he reigned over Judah seven years and six months: and in Jerusalem he reigned thirty and three years over all Israel and Judah.", insight:"Thirty-three years in Jerusalem; the city of David became the heart of the nation."},
{q:"Who held Jerusalem when David came?", options:["The Jebusites","The Philistines","The Canaanites of Gezer","The Amorites"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 5:6",verse:"And the king and his men went to Jerusalem unto the Jebusites, the inhabitants of the land: which spake unto David, saying, Except thou take away the blind and the lame, thou shalt not come in hither: thinking, David cannot come in hither.", insight:"The Jebusites held the fortress; the last stronghold fell to the king who trusted God."},
{q:"What was the Jebusites' taunt?", options:["Except thou take away the blind and the lame, thou shalt not come in hither","Thy army is too small","The walls reach to heaven","Our gods will defend us"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 5:6",verse:"And the king and his men went to Jerusalem unto the Jebusites, the inhabitants of the land: which spake unto David, saying, Except thou take away the blind and the lame, thou shalt not come in hither: thinking, David cannot come in hither.", insight:"They mocked with the blind and the lame; contempt for the weak became their epitaph."},
{q:"What stronghold did David take?", options:["The strong hold of Zion","The tower of Shechem","The fortress of Gibeon","The walls of Jericho"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 5:7",verse:"Nevertheless David took the strong hold of Zion: the same is the city of David.", insight:"The strong hold of Zion; the unconquered fortress fell, and David made it his own."},
{q:"What did David call the fort?", options:["The city of David","The city of God","New Jerusalem","The holy hill"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 5:9",verse:"So David dwelt in the fort, and called it the city of David. And David built round about from Millo and inward.", insight:"The city of David; he gave his name to the place God gave him."},
{q:"What did David build round about?", options:["From Millo and inward","A wall to the sea","A temple of cedar","Towers on every hill"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 5:9",verse:"So David dwelt in the fort, and called it the city of David. And David built round about from Millo and inward.", insight:"From Millo inward; the king built out from the stronghold, securing what God had given."},
{q:"What did David perceive about his kingdom?", options:["That the LORD had established him king, and exalted his kingdom for his people Israel's sake","That the Philistines feared him","That his sons would reign forever","That the elders loved him"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 5:12",verse:"And David perceived that the LORD had established him king over Israel, and that he had exalted his kingdom for his people Israel’s sake.", insight:"For his people Israel's sake; David knew the throne was not about him but about them."},
{q:"Who sent cedar trees, carpenters, and masons to David?", options:["Hiram king of Tyre","The king of Egypt","The lords of the Philistines","The king of Moab"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 5:11",verse:"And Hiram king of Tyre sent messengers to David, and cedar trees, and carpenters, and masons: and they built David an house.", insight:"Hiram of Tyre sent builders; foreign kings honored the king whom God had lifted."},
{q:"Which of these sons was born to David in Jerusalem?", options:["Solomon","Absalom","Amnon","Adonijah"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 5:14",verse:"And these be the names of those that were born unto him in Jerusalem; Shammuah, and Shobab, and Nathan, and Solomon,", insight:"Solomon was born in Jerusalem; the son of peace was born in the city of peace."},
{q:"Where did the Philistines spread themselves?", options:["In the valley of Rephaim","On the plain of Sharon","At the brook Besor","In the wilderness of Ziph"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 5:18",verse:"The Philistines also came and spread themselves in the valley of Rephaim.", insight:"The valley of Rephaim; the old enemy came to test the new king, and David asked God first."},
{q:"What did the LORD answer when David enquired about the Philistines?", options:["Go up, for I will doubtless deliver them into thine hand","Flee to the hold and hide","Make peace with them","Wait until the harvest"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 5:19",verse:"And David enquired of the LORD, saying, Shall I go up to the Philistines? wilt thou deliver them into mine hand? And the LORD said unto David, Go up: for I will doubtless deliver the Philistines into thine hand.", insight:"'Go up, I will doubtless deliver them'; David asked before he fought, and God answered plainly."},
{q:"What sound was David to wait for in the second battle?", options:["The sound of a going in the tops of the mulberry trees","The blowing of the trumpets","The shouting of his men","The thunder from heaven"], a:0, ref:"2 Samuel 5:24",verse:"And let it be, when thou hearest the sound of a going in the tops of the mulberry trees, that then thou shalt bestir thyself: for then shall the LORD go out before thee, to smite the host of the Philistines.", insight:"The sound of marching in the mulberry tops; God goes before His people, and the wise wait for His step."}
]}
]);
